The pragmatic-console crate bundles two typefaces, as unmodified Latin
subsets, and embeds them in the pages it renders (and so do the pragmatic
CLI and Pragmatic Server, which serve them):

- EB Garamond, roman and italic, as Google Fonts distributes them
  (crates/pragmatic-console/assets/fonts/eb-garamond-latin.woff2,
  eb-garamond-italic-latin.woff2),
  Copyright 2017 The EB Garamond Project Authors
  (https://github.com/octaviopardo/EBGaramond12),
  licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
  (crates/pragmatic-console/assets/fonts/OFL-EBGaramond.txt).

- IBM Plex Mono, regular and medium, as IBM distributes them in the
  @ibm/plex-mono 2.5.0 package
  (crates/pragmatic-console/assets/fonts/IBMPlexMono-Regular-Latin1.woff2,
  IBMPlexMono-Medium-Latin1.woff2),
  Copyright (c) 2017 IBM Corp. with Reserved Font Name "Plex",
  licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1
  (crates/pragmatic-console/assets/fonts/OFL-IBMPlexMono.txt).
